of the task, recorded in the provider\'s audit log (HCP 5.2.1, 8.2). The maxLength is a framework bound, not an HCP requirement."},"maxEntries":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"HCP `maxEntries`: the most entries to return. Absent means HCP\'s default of 5. A ceiling, not a target: the provider returns at most the lesser of this value and 20, and never pads to reach it (HCP 5.2.1, 7.2)."},"accessToken":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":8192,"description":"The HCP access token that stands for the grant (an OAuth or first-party token, HCP 12, 13), carried unchanged. HCP\'s HTTP binding sends it as a Bearer token (HCP 9.3); HCP leaves how authorization evidence is carried to each binding (HCP 1.2), and this member carries it in the document. The provider validates it exactly as over HTTP and treats it as opaque."}},"\$defs":{"Category":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2048,"pattern":"^([a-z][a-z0-9_]*|[a-zA-Z][a-zA-Z0-9+.-]*:\\\\S+)\$","description":"An HCP context category (HCP 4.5), the primary unit of access control: either a slug from HCP\'s category registry, such as `general_preferences` or `health_context`, or a custom category written as an absolute URI under a domain its definer controls. A custom category is not portable between providers without bilateral agreement (HCP 4.5)."},"PurposeCode":{"type":"string","format":"uri","minLength":1,"maxLength":2048,"pattern":"^[a-zA-Z][a-zA-Z0-9+.-]*:\\\\S+\$","description":"An HCP purpose code: an absolute URI naming the purpose for which context is requested or may be used (HCP 6.1.5.2)."}}}';

