,"description":"When it was converted."},"convertedBy":{"type":"string","maxLength":2048,"description":"Who converted it."},"unmapped":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true,"description":"v1 members the conversion did not map."}}},"metadata":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true,"description":"Free-form data the implementation attaches for its own purposes; carries no HCP meaning (HCP 4.2)."}}},"Relationship":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true,"required":["type","target","assertedBy","recordedAt"],"description":"A relationship from this entry to another (HCP 4.2.3). Only a `contradicts` relationship may carry a `proposal` (HCP 4.7.4), which is a `RecordedProposal`, as HCP defines it. This rule is stated here and not as a schema conditional: the registry\'s Rust generator does not support `if`/`then`/`else`, so a validator does not check it.","properties":{"type":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/RelationshipType","description":"The kind of relationship."},"target":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2048,"description":"The related entry\'s `id`."},"assertedBy":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true,"required":["role","id"],"description":"Who asserted the relationship.","properties":{"role":{"type":"string","enum":["management-client","context-client","authorization-service","hcp-provider"],"description":"Their role (HCP 3.9). HCP\'s own values, carried verbatim."},"id":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2048,"description":"Their identifier."}}},"recordedAt":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Instant","description":"When the provider recorded the relationship."},"proposal":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/RecordedProposal","description":"A proposal for resolving a conflict, which changes nothing until the Context Subject acts (HCP 4.7.4)."}}},"RecordedProposal":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true,"required":["act","entry","rationale","weighed","proposedBy","proposedAt"],"description":"A proposal for resolving a conflict, as the provider records it on a `contradicts` relationship (HCP 4.7.4). It changes nothing until the Context Subject acts. It is the `Proposal` a client writes (entry-write.schema.json), with `proposedBy` and `proposedAt`, which the provider sets and never takes from a request (HCP 4.7.4). A proposal is never disclosed to a Context Client (HCP 7.4). Open, as HCP\'s own shape is.","properties":{"act":{"type":"string","enum":["reject","accept","supersede"],"description":"The act proposed (HCP 4.7.3, 4.7.4). HCP\'s own values, carried verbatim."},"entry":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2048,"description":"The entry the act applies to (HCP 4.7.4). The maxLength is a framework bound, not an HCP requirement."},"rationale":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":4096,"description":"Why, in words the Context Subject can read (HCP 4.7.4). The maxLength is a framework bound, not an HCP requirement."},"weighed":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"maxItems":64,"items":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2048},"description":"What the proposal considered: an open set, of which HCP defines `basis`, `declarationType`, `standing`, `permittedPurposes`, `recency` and `confidence` (HCP 4.7.4). The maxItems and maxLength are framework bounds, not HCP requirements."},"proposedBy":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true,"required":["role","id"],"description":"Who made the proposal: the provider under the Memory Manager Profile, or the client that asserted the conflict (HCP 4.7.4, 15). Set by the provider, never taken from a request.","properties":{"role":{"type":"string","enum":["management-client","context-client","authorization-service","hcp-provider"],"description":"Their role (HCP 3.9). HCP\'s own values, carried verbatim."},"id":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2048,"description":"Their identifier. The maxLength is a framework bound, not an HCP requirement."}}},"proposedAt":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Instant","description":"When the provider recorded the proposal (HCP 4.7.4). Set by the provider, never taken from a request."}}},"RelationshipType":{"type":"string","enum":["derivedFrom","supersedes","contradicts","duplicates"],"description":"How one entry relates to another (HCP 4.2.3). HCP\'s own values, carried verbatim."},"Provenance":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true,"required":["assertedBy","assertedAt","source","submittedByClient","authorizedUnder","recordedByProvider","recordedAt"],"description":"The provenance of one version of an entry (HCP 4.2, 3.5).","properties":{"assertedBy":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true,"required":["id","assurance"],"description":"The Context Asserter (HCP 3.5, 3.6).","properties":{"id":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2048,"description":"The Context Asserter\'s identifier."},"assurance":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Assurance","description":"How the asserter\'s identity was established."},"via":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true,"required":["kind","id"],"description":"Present only where a client attested for an issuer under the issuer\'s authorization (HCP 3.7).","properties":{"kind":{"type":"string","enum":["authorization-credential","arrangement"],"description":"What the client attested under. HCP\'s own values, carried verbatim."},"id":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2048,"description":"The identifier of the attestation authorization or the recorded arrangement."}}}}},"assertedAt":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Instant","description":"When the assertion was made, as the submitting client states it."},"source":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2048,"description":"The origin of the entry, as the submitting client states it: a conversation or document identifier, `person-input` or `integration` (HCP 4.2)."},"submittedByClient":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/ClientDescription","description":"The HCP Client that submitted this version, and its Client Operator (HCP 3.5)."},"authorizedUnder":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2048,"description":"The grant under which this version was written."},