type the provider does not recognize is preserved and never raises assurance (HCP A.3). An item whose type is `verifiable-credential` MUST carry `credential`, an object with `@context`, `type`, `issuer` and `credentialSubject`, held whole as its issuer secured it (HCP 4.2.2). This rule is stated here and not as a schema conditional: the registry\'s Rust generator does not support `if`/`then`/`else`, so a validator does not check it.","properties":{"role":{"type":"string","enum":["content","supports"],"description":"`content`: the item\'s credential is the entry\'s content (VC Evidence profile). `supports`: the item backs content stated elsewhere in the entry (HCP 4.2.2)."},"type":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2048,"description":"The evidence type: `verifiable-credential`, or a URI (HCP 4.2.2, A.3)."},"credential":{"description":"The credential: for `verifiable-credential`, a W3C Verifiable Credential with `@context`, `type`, `issuer` and `credentialSubject`, whose own data model governs its contents (HCP 4.2.2, 14.2)."},"verification":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true,"required":["result","at"],"description":"The provider\'s record of its most recent verification of the credential (HCP 4.2.2). Set only by the provider.","properties":{"result":{"type":"string","enum":["verified","failed"],"description":"The outcome."},"at":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Instant","description":"When the provider verified."},"by":{"type":"string","enum":["provider","trust-domain"],"description":"Who verified: the provider, or the Context Subject\'s trust domain under end-to-end encrypted storage (HCP 4.8). HCP\'s own values, carried verbatim."}}}}},"Classification":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true,"required":["categories"],"description":"HCP\'s classification of the entry (HCP 4.2, 4.5). A grant reaches an entry when it covers any one of the entry\'s categories (HCP 4.5).","properties":{"categories":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"uniqueItems":true,"items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Category"},"description":"One or more categories, without duplicates (HCP 4.2, 4.5). In a disclosure, only the categories the requesting grant covers (HCP 7.4)."},"dimension":{"type":["string","null"],"maxLength":2048,"description":"A free-form identifier of the dimension the entry addresses, scoped within its categories: a hint for conflict detection that grants and limits nothing (HCP 4.2)."},"permittedPurposes":{"type":"array","uniqueItems":true,"items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/PurposeCode"},"description":"The Authorizing Principal\'s narrowing of the entry\'s purposes; absent means no limit (HCP 4.2.6)."}}},"PurposeCode":{"type":"string","format":"uri","minLength":1,"maxLength":2048,"pattern":"^[a-zA-Z][a-zA-Z0-9+.-]*:\\\\S+\$","description":"An HCP purpose code: an absolute URI naming the purpose for which context is requested or may be used (HCP 6.1.5.2)."},"Assertion":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true,"required":["declarationType"],"description":"What the submitting client states about the assertion (HCP 4.2). `confidence` is REQUIRED and non-null when `declarationType` is `model-inferred`, and null or absent otherwise (HCP 4.2, 4.4). This rule is stated here and not as a schema conditional: the registry\'s Rust generator does not support `if`/`then`/`else`, so a validator does not check it.","properties":{"declarationType":{"type":"string","enum":["person-declared","model-inferred","issuer-attested"],"description":"What kind of party made the assertion (HCP 4.4); never omitted. HCP\'s own values, carried verbatim."},"confidence":{"type":["string","null"],"enum":["high","medium","low",null],"description":"How confident an inferring model is (HCP 4.2, 4.4)."},"validUntil":{"type":["string","null"],"format":"date-time","description":"The instant after which the content no longer holds; absent or null means it does not expire (HCP 4.2). Not the instant after which a disclosed copy stops being usable, which is a disclosure\'s `useUntil` (HCP 7.6)